# Python dependencies for ansible-role-vault
# Source file for pip-compile. DO NOT edit requirements.txt directly.
#
# REGENERATE REPRODUCIBLY:
#
#   docker run --rm --platform linux/amd64 -v "$PWD:/w" -w /w python:3.11-slim \
#     sh -c 'pip install -q --require-hashes -r requirements-generator.txt && \
#            pip-compile --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements.txt requirements.in'
#
# Three things make that reproducible, each measured rather than assumed.
#
# 1. THE PLATFORM. --generate-hashes enumerates the wheels the resolver can SEE,
#    which depends on OS, architecture and Python version. CI is ubuntu-latest
#    x86_64 / Python 3.11; regenerating on macOS rewrote ~184 lines for no
#    semantic reason.
#
# 2. THE EXISTING OUTPUT FILE. Run against the existing requirements.txt, never
#    a fresh path. pip-compile honours the pins already in its output file, so an
#    unrelated transitive is not silently upgraded -- a fresh-path run pulled
#    urllib3 2.8.0, which was ONE DAY OLD and inside the 7-day cooldown floor
#    .github/dependabot.yml sets precisely to catch a malicious or yanked
#    upstream release. Upgrades belong to Dependabot, which enforces that floor.
#
# 3. THE WHOLE GENERATOR TOOLCHAIN, not just pip-tools. See
#    requirements-generator.in: `pip install pip-tools==7.6.1` admits more than
#    one Click, and Click's version changes the generated header. pip is pinned
#    there too -- pip is the resolver, and the python:3.11-slim tag is mutable,
#    so the base image's bundled pip is not a fixed input either.
#
# THE `--no-index` IN THE GENERATED HEADER WAS NEVER PASSED AND NEVER REACHED
# PIP. Do not "fix" the documented command to match it, and do not pass it: the
# lock would then be resolved from whatever happens to be in the local cache.
#
#   It is a rendering artifact of Click 8.5.0, the pinned version.
#   piptools/utils.py::get_compile_command skips an option when
#   `option.default == value`. Click 8.5.0 reports the --no-index default as
#   `Sentinel.UNSET`, so `UNSET == False` is False, the guard never fires, and
#   -- with no secondary `--index` opt to switch to -- the emitter falls to
#   `arg = option_long_name` and prints the flag despite its False value.
#   Click 8.4.1 and 8.1.7 report that default as False, the guard fires, and the
#   same pip-tools emits NO such line. That version-dependence is why the
#   toolchain is pinned as a whole.
#
#   Evidence it was never in effect: in a fresh container with an empty pip cache
#   and `--network none`, pip-compile FAILS with
#   "DistributionNotFound: No matching distribution found for hvac>=2.0.0".
#   Resolution requires the index; with --no-index genuinely active it could not
#   have succeeded with the network up either.
#
# Classification: UNCLASSIFIED

# HashiCorp Vault API client - required by community.hashi_vault collection
# https://pypi.org/project/hvac/
# Supports Vault v1.4.7+, Python 3.8+
hvac>=2.0.0

# Address classification used by ansible.utils.ipaddr in tasks/preflight/dns.yml.
# The collection declares netaddr>=0.10.1; it is a CONTROLLER-side requirement.
netaddr>=0.10.1
